Description: pick a concrete libcurl4-dev provider in Build-Depends
 `debian/control` bare-lists `libcurl4-dev` as a Build-Depends.  That
 name is a virtual package with three concrete providers in Debian:
 .
   libcurl4-openssl-dev
   libcurl4-gnutls-dev
   libcurl4-nss-dev
 .
 When none of these is already installed and apt is asked to install
 the virtual name from the CLI, `apt-get` refuses to pick — the CLI
 isn't a stable interface for picking among alternative providers, and
 the operator-facing message is:
 .
   E: Package 'libcurl4-dev' has no installation candidate
 .
 Our source-build runs `apt-get build-dep` non-interactively inside a
 clean container, so this is a hard fail-stop.  Captured during
 Athena's GROUPS-01 phase 3 gnome build 2026-05-14 — llvm-toolchain-15
 is pulled in transitively as a build-dep of some package in the
 gnome closure (likely through clang / mesa's optional toolchain).
 .
 The fix follows standard Debian practice for build-depending on a
 virtual: alternation with a concrete preference first.
 `libcurl4-openssl-dev` is chosen because (a) it's the de-facto
 default across Debian packages that use libcurl, (b) the TLS backend
 matches the rest of our build container (libssl3 is already in
 base_include), and (c) llvm's curl integration doesn't require any
 gnutls/nss-specific features.  Keeping `| libcurl4-dev` as the
 second alternative means a system that *already* has one of the
 other providers installed still satisfies the build-dep without a
 second concrete install.
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-14
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@
     llvm-spirv-15 [ amd64 arm64 armel armhf mips64el mipsel ppc64el riscv64 s390x ] <!stage1> |
     llvm-spirv-14 [ amd64 arm64 armel armhf mips64el mipsel ppc64el riscv64 s390x ] <!stage1> | hello [!i386],
     spirv-tools [ linux-any ] | hello [ !i386],
-    libcurl4-dev,
+    libcurl4-openssl-dev | libcurl4-dev,
     libgrpc++-dev [amd64 arm64 armel armhf mips64el mipsel ppc64 ppc64el powerpc riscv64 s390x],
     protobuf-compiler-grpc [amd64 arm64 armel armhf mips64el mipsel ppc64 ppc64el powerpc riscv64 s390x],
     libprotobuf-dev [amd64 arm64 armel armhf mips64el mipsel ppc64 ppc64el powerpc riscv64 s390x],
